</div>
<div id="lstnumberx91" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx91.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">internal_score</span><span id="lstnumberx91.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx91.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx91.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">0.62615377</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the next case (Figure <a href="#A3.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ C.2. Patch Validation Decisions: False Positives ‣ Appendix C Patch Validation Prompts ‣ Abstain and Validate: A Dual-LLM Policy for Reducing Noise in Agentic Program Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), the bug report provides relatively high-level discussion of the issue but does not specify what property should be used to check for links for a test sequencer module.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The ground-truth patch adds conditional handling based on the presence of a particular field (ts_version) in an input row. The agent’s patch modifies this into an if-else statement. The else branch is equivalent to the fall-through case in the ground-truth patch. However, the if guard checks a different field (archive_file), which it inferred from the existing test files.</p>
</div>
