</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>Patch Validation Decisions: True Positives</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the two bugs below, the agent patch is able to pass the held-out ground-truth reproduction test. Additionally, manual inspection shows these are equivalent to the changes made in the ground-truth patch.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first bug (Figure <a href="#A3.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ C.3. Patch Validation Decisions: True Positives ‣ Appendix C Patch Validation Prompts ‣ Abstain and Validate: A Dual-LLM Policy for Reducing Noise in Agentic Program Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) requires that the agent add an emptiness check to avoid processing cases where there are no child tasks. The ground-truth patch tightens a guard to add this check.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F17" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
