</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the next example (Figure <a href="#A3.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ C.3. Patch Validation Decisions: True Positives ‣ Appendix C Patch Validation Prompts ‣ Abstain and Validate: A Dual-LLM Policy for Reducing Noise in Agentic Program Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), the bug description provides instructions on the expected edits to a calculation. The ground-truth patch updates the calculation and in addition removes a constant that is no longer used. The agent patch <em id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only</em> updates the calculation, but does so in the correct way.</p>
</div>
